fficulty, but C's unwillingness to further education is a bigger red flag for adaptability. She could argue that B's technical competence (weather, computer) is more relevant for long-haul, and his stress handling is proven. She could maintain B.\n\nWe need to produce a short argumentative contribution, referencing prior discussion, using explicit facts, and give vote. Let's keep B.\n\nWe'll say: \"I understand the panel's emphasis on C's reliability and calmness, but I remain convinced B is the better overall fit because his conscientiousness ensures reliability, his stress handling is proven, his technical competence (weather assessment, computer) is directly relevant, and his communication issues, while present, are less likely to undermine crew cooperation than C's egocentric attitude and unwillingness to further education.\" Provide evidence: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; C difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Conclude vote B.\n\nNow output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
